# Sealround web app. From apps/web: Copy-Item .env.example .env.local, then edit. See README.md.
#
# Every variable here starts with NEXT_PUBLIC_, so its value is compiled into
# the JavaScript every visitor downloads. Nothing in this file is secret, and
# nothing secret may ever be put in it (see NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_ACCOUNTS below).
# Next.js reads the file when the dev server starts or the app is built:
# restart `next dev` after changing it.
#
# With everything commented out (the default) the app runs in MOCK MODE: a
# simulated chain and wallet in the browser, no network, no funds.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosts (either mode)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The app's own origin when the landing page and the app run on two hosts of
# one deployment (example.com and app.example.com; see src/proxy.ts). With it,
# landing-page links point here and app paths on the landing host redirect
# here. Leave it unset on a single host: the app is then under /sales.
# Locally, http://app.localhost:3000 already serves the app at / without it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://app.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEAR mode: set the contract and the app talks to a real chain.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The deployed Sealround contract account. Setting this switches NEAR mode on;
# leaving it empty keeps mock mode, whatever else is set.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FAIRGROUND_CONTRACT=fairground.testnet

# testnet (default) | mainnet | sandbox (a local chain, see README.md).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_NETWORK=testnet

# JSON-RPC endpoint for views. Defaults: https://rpc.testnet.near.org,
# https://rpc.mainnet.near.org, http://127.0.0.1:3030 (sandbox). The public
# endpoints are rate limited; use your own provider's URL for a real launch.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.near.org

# The USDC (NEP-141) contract new sales are paid in, and the one balances,
# storage registration and the test faucet use. It must be in the contract's
# allowed_quote_tokens and in the relayer's USDC_CONTRACTS.
# Defaults: usdc.fakes.testnet (testnet, open mint) and Circle's
# 17208628f84f5d6ad33f0da3bbbeb27ffcb398eac501a31bd6ad2011e36133a1 (mainnet).
# Required on a sandbox (the mock-ft account you deployed).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USDC_CONTRACT=usdc.fakes.testnet

# Base URL of the gas relayer (apps/relayer), absolute or a same-origin path.
# With it, bids, claims, reveals, clear_onchain and refund mode are gasless
# for wallets that can sign NEP-366 delegates. Without it every call is a
# normal transaction the user pays for. The relayer's CORS_ORIGINS must list
# this app's origin.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAYER_URL=http://localhost:8787

# sha256 of the reproducible sealer build (enclave/res/fairground_sealer.wasm.sha256),
# 64 hex characters. The app compares it with the code hash the contract pinned
# and shows whether they match. Optional; without it that check cannot pass.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SEALER_CODE_HASH=f8408a875ec685394d00937cfc320c8b5e8c2a1e8398cfdf34987aa91001d8cb

# 1Click partner JWT for the same-origin quote and status proxy. Server only.
# ONECLICK_JWT=

# Live deposit quotes are off by default. Set to 1 only for a mainnet
# deployment configured to receive Circle's native USDC on NEAR.
# ONECLICK_REAL_SWAPS=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local sandbox only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Accounts the app can sign for without a wallet, with their FULL-ACCESS secret
# keys: <account_id>=ed25519:<secret>, separated by commas.
#
# These keys end up in the browser bundle. The app only uses them when
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_NETWORK is "sandbox" AND the RPC URL is on localhost or
# 127.0.0.1; on any other network they are dropped when the config is read and
# refused again when a signer is built. Still: never put a testnet or mainnet
# key here, and never set this variable in a deployed environment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_ACCOUNTS=alice.test.near=ed25519:...,bob.test.near=ed25519:...

# A complete sandbox example (the accounts are whatever your setup script made):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FAIRGROUND_CONTRACT=fairground.test.near
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_NETWORK=sandbox
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3030
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USDC_CONTRACT=usdc.test.near
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAYER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_ACCOUNTS=alice.test.near=ed25519:...,bob.test.near=ed25519:...
